### SeatLock: click "Send Request" above each block (needs the REST Client extension).
### Run them top to bottom. Start the API and seed the database first.

@base = http://localhost:8000

### Health check
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Register a user (409 the second time is fine)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "riya@example.com", "password": "password123"}

### 2. Log in (the token is reused automatically below)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "riya@example.com", "password": "password123"}

### 3. List events
GET {{base}}/events

### 4. Seat map of event 1
GET {{base}}/events/1/seats

### 5. Hold seats 1 and 2 (run it twice: the second time you get the SAME booking back, status 200)
# @name hold
POST {{base}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-hold-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id": 1, "seat_ids": [1, 2]}

### 6. Pay for the booking
POST {{base}}/bookings/{{hold.response.body.id}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-pay-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{"payment_token": "tok_success"}

### 7. My bookings
GET {{base}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 8. Cancel it (seats become free again)
POST {{base}}/bookings/{{hold.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
